--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFV §31: the chunk phase of the layout, a selection sort by Lemma 12 exchanges*: After the single-bit moves (`KFV25Moves`) the `N = D q` chunks of `K` bits are in axis-major
--   order; Lemma 16's layout wants them chunk-major. Position `t` of the target holds the chunk
--   originally at `src t = (t mod D) q + ⌊t / D⌋`. Selection sort: at step `t` the wanted chunk sits
--   at the *chase* position `x_t`: start at `src t` and apply `src` while the value is `< t`
--   (`chF`, fuel `N`); exchange positions `t` and `x_t` (nothing if equal). At most `N` exchanges,
--   and the positions are computed by a fixed arithmetic loop, so a fixed program can do it.
--
